DECISIONS 282, CODEGEN.md §5.13: a default that does not fold and whose type takes an argument (the
earlier field ev) is computed, so types mode refuses it like L's own default reading its parameter. (A
dependent map's key was the other case: only go types read one, which is E8019 `unbuilt` since
DECISIONS 320, and a cpp types decoder reads no map.)
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Ev.
record Ev {
  /// Max.
  max: Int = 5
}

/// Evs.
let evs: table Ev = { a {}, b { max: 7 } }

/// L.
record L(e: Ev) {
  /// Its event's max.
  top: Int = e.max
}

/// R.
record R {
  /// Ev.
  ev: ref evs
  /// L of ev.
  l: L(ev) = {}
  /// Many, none by default: a constant.
  ls: [L(ev)] = []
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8014]  a/a.canon:15:3
  types mode cannot emit the computed default of L.top: there is no data to read it from

error[E8014]  a/a.canon:23:3
  types mode cannot emit the computed default of R.l: there is no data to read it from

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
